== (2) uniqueness of the root Y of F(discPt d X Y) = 0 (F = Fq of p21_46, the plane quartic)
  (a) the criterion as stated: dF/d(dependent coordinate) at the residue point odd for every X mod 2
  (b) the certificate used: G(X, Y) = F(discPt d X Y) = 2^m G1(X, Y), 2^m = the 2-part of the content of G, and
      G1(X, Y) - G1(X, Y') = (Y - Y') H(X, Y, Y') with H in Z[X, Y, Y'] odd at every residue: then G(X, .) has at most one root in Z_2
  disc 1: (a) dF/dy at discPt d X Y mod 2 = Mod(1, 2), values at (X, Y) mod 2 [1, 1, 1, 1]: odd; residue point [0, 0, 1] singular mod 2 (all partials even): 0
